3. System-provided link dependencies and binary distribution
-----------------------------------------------------------
tools/build.py copies development static archives selected by pkg-config into
ignored build/native/: libuv; OpenSSL libssl/libcrypto; c-ares; Brotli encoder,
decoder and common; Zstandard; and nghttp2. The exact package versions and
archive hashes depend on the builder's environment. silk.toml also declares
dynamic zlib, resolver, pthread, and math libraries. These system packages
are not source-vendored here and are not assigned fictitious fixed versions.
SQLite is not a system dependency: the db-sqlite package of silk-lang/lib-sqlite,
pinned by commit in silk.toml, compiles the SQLite amalgamation that package
pins by SHA-256 into the executable.

Upstream project/license references (the installed version's terms govern):
  libuv: https://github.com/libuv/libuv (MIT and retained per-file notices)
  OpenSSL: https://github.com/openssl/openssl (version-specific license)
  c-ares: https://github.com/c-ares/c-ares (MIT and retained notices)
  Brotli: https://github.com/google/brotli (MIT)
